Package: flatcor
Title: Objective Bayes for Linear Regression with Flat Correlations
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Diemithry M.", "Kloppenburg", email = "diemithrykloppenburg@hotmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Bayes factors and estimation for linear regression with
    objective priors that extend Jeffreys' flat correlation to several
    predictors. The default makes every correlation matrix of the outcome and
    predictors equally likely: R-squared ~ Beta(k/2, 1) (as rstanarm stan_lm
    with eta = 1), and each coefficient's partial correlation is flat for any
    number of predictors, so testing one coefficient is Jeffreys' correlation
    test with or without covariates. The alternative, flat-R, is flat on the
    multiple correlation R for every number of predictors (R-squared ~
    Beta(1/2, 1)). Both are mixtures of Zellner g-priors with closed-form Bayes
    factors that need only R-squared, n and k; estimation samples the prior in
    its own coordinates (R and a direction) with Stan.
